<p>When a hailstorm or windstorm hits a commercial property, the damage is rarely limited to one roof. It can involve multiple buildings, rooftop equipment, tenant spaces, parking structures, and lost income at the same time. Dallas Public Adjuster represents owners and managers on <strong>commercial property insurance claims in Dallas</strong>, Dallas County, and nearby North Texas cities. We help organize the documentation, prepare detailed estimates, and handle communication with the insurer so you can focus on tenants and operations.</p>

<h2>Commercial Properties We Represent</h2>
<h3>Apartment complexes</h3>
<p>Multi-building complexes can sustain different levels of damage from building to building, with roof, siding, window, and interior water losses all in one claim. Tenant displacement and rental income add more moving parts. During the August 2022 flash flood, NOAA reports note that 2 feet of water entered an east Dallas apartment complex, a reminder that flood and storm damage can arrive together.</p>
<h3>Retail and office buildings</h3>
<p>Strip centers, medical offices, and office buildings often have flat or low-slope roofs, storefront glazing, signage, and HVAC units that can all be damaged in one event. Business interruption for tenants and owners can be part of the picture.</p>
<h3>Warehouses and industrial facilities</h3>
<p>Large low-slope roofs, metal panels, skylights, overhead doors, and stored inventory create big exposure. On May 28, 2024, NOAA records describe a roof torn from a commercial building in Carrollton and a partial roof collapse in Pleasant Grove during severe straight-line winds.</p>
<h3>HOA and multi-family communities</h3>
<p>Associations must coordinate the master policy, governing documents, a board, and individual owners. Clear documentation by building and by unit helps keep a complicated claim organized.</p>

<h2>Common Causes of Commercial Losses in North Texas</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hail</strong> damaging TPO and modified-bitumen membranes, metal roofs and wall panels, rooftop HVAC units, skylights, and vehicles. See <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Wind</strong> lifting roof membranes and edge metal, breaking glass, and toppling signs. See <a href="/services/wind-damage-claims/">wind damage claims</a>.</li>
