<h2>Our Approach to Commercial Claims</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Policy and lease review.</strong> We read the full commercial policy and, where relevant, how leases assign responsibility for repairs and insurance.</li>
<li><strong>Building-by-building inspection.</strong> We document roofs, rooftop equipment, envelopes, interiors, and site features, using Matterport 3D imaging where it helps.</li>
<li><strong>Detailed estimating.</strong> We prepare Xactimate estimates with line items for each building and system, and coordinate with engineers or specialty contractors when needed.</li>
<li><strong>Business income documentation.</strong> We help organize the records the insurer will ask for to evaluate lost income or rent.</li>
<li><strong>Presentation and negotiation.</strong> We present the claim, respond to the insurer’s questions, and track deadlines. If there is a disagreement on the amount of loss, <a href="/services/insurance-appraisal/">insurance appraisal</a> may be an option under your policy.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Why Commercial Claims Are Often Underpaid</h2>
<p>Large losses invite shortcuts. An insurer’s estimate may treat a full membrane replacement as a patch, miss damaged insulation under a wet roof, skip rooftop units, or apply pricing that does not reflect current Dallas-area costs. Multi-building claims can also leave whole structures out of the scope. A careful <a href="/services/insurance-estimate-review/">estimate review</a> can show where the numbers differ and why.</p>

<h2>Working With Dallas Public Adjuster</h2>
<p>We represent the insured only. We do not perform repairs on claims we adjust, and we do not give legal advice. If a dispute involves litigation, bad faith, or a deadline to sue, consult a Texas attorney. Nobody can guarantee a commercial settlement, but a complete, well-organized claim gives the insurer the information it needs to evaluate the loss.</p>
<p>Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement. To discuss a commercial loss, request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a>.</p>
